    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Preferred Servers are file shares that Ivanti Neurons uses to provide files, without needing Ivanti software on the host machine. They matter because devices can retrieve content from a local or controlled location. You configure a server name, URL or file path, read credentials, and optionally an SMB path for sync engines. HTTPS is recommended because it encrypts data; HTTP sends data in plain text. Preferred Server: content share. Read credentials: access account. SMB path: sync-engine location.",
      "id": "0c1d9abd-bed1-4211-b7c2-60db4902867b",
